    "result_text": "I implemented the PENDING / approve / reject flow, and `bin/e2e` passes (`approvals` \u2713). The app log shows no errors.\n\n**What it does now**\n- **Settling:** when a clerk settles a claim whose due is above the clerk limit, the claim becomes **PENDING** and the audit gets `CLAIM_PENDING \u2026`. Its due stays live and isn't fixed yet. Stewards, and claims within the limit, still settle as before. The screen no longer blocks the settle itself.\n- **Approve** (steward only, PENDING claims only): the opener can't approve their own claim. The due is worked out and fixed at the moment of approval. The claim becomes SETTLED and the audit gets `CLAIM_APPROVED \u2026 due=<due>`.\n- **Reject** (steward only, PENDING claims only, a reason is required): the claim goes back to OPEN and the audit gets `CLAIM_REJECTED \u2026 reason=<reason>`.\n- **Totals:** a PENDING claim counts as open everywhere. That covers claimed and due totals, overdue, the rule that leaves out a held person's open claims, and the due-total fixed when a period is closed. This applies on both the server and the screen.\n- **Screen:** each claim row has new `claim-approve` and `claim-reject` buttons and a `claim-reject-reason` box. Any refusal shows `claim-error` and writes nothing, and typing a new reason clears the old error.\n\n**Server changes**\n- I moved the due calculation into a shared `ClaimDue` so settling and approving work it out the same way.\n- New endpoints: `approve.POST.yml` and `reject.POST.yml`. A non-steward is refused with 403 via `NotStewardException`.\n- No database migration was needed: the existing status column already fits `PENDING`. The rejection reason is only written to the audit file, not stored on the claim.\n- I removed `ClerkLimitException`, its handler and its escalation YAML, since nothing raises it any more.\n\n**One fix outside the request:** re-loading a sheet showed the current-sheet marker (`sheet-current-id`) straight away, before the fresh data had arrived. The test then took the old status as its starting point and read the incoming refresh as the action going through: Vic's self-approval looked accepted even though the server had refused it. The marker now hides until the re-read finishes (in `features/session/sheet.slot.tsx`), so a reload always ends showing what the store holds.\n\n**Choices the request didn't specify:** a PENDING claim can't be voided or settled again. Only a steward can reject, but the opener is allowed to reject their own claim; only approving is blocked for them.",
